                <pb facs="0721" n="711" xml:id="pg711"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/1–2947: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Stuart</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-01-29">January 29,
                        1947</date>.<lb/>[Received January 29—6:30 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>160. I called on Generalissimo at 4:30 and informed him of decision to withdraw
                    Executive Headquarters. Wang Ping-nan, representing Communist delegation, was
                    informed at 5:30. Announcement was made by Embassy to press at 6:00 p.m.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stuart</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
